{
  "_notes": "ReefTank layout (P1.1). Coordinates are design pixels at 1920x1080 inside the camera Group; ReefTank scales the camera by screen width / design.width. layers run back to front, each built as a Group whose id is the layer id; name is the PRD scene-stack label. parallax is the per-layer drift factor P1.2 applies to the camera offset (0 = fixed, 1 = moves with the camera); the values here are placeholders. drift (P1.2) is the camera loop: amplitude is in design px and the validator rejects an amplitude where parallax * amplitude exceeds the art margin of a decor that spans the view (the 2560-wide sand_lip in foreground has 320 px of margin at parallax 1.0, so amplitude x stays at or under 320; nothing spans the view vertically, so y stays 0). A layer with a lane block is a fish lane: rect bounds the fish anchor, scale and tint (0xRRGGBBAA multiply) set the lane's depth. decor (P1.7 art, placed by P1.8 from docs/art/placement-proposal.json, ids are the proposal keys): the painted backdrop sits in waterGradient with 313 px of drift margin on each side; the mid coral tiles and rock pillar in midCoral hide back-lane fish; the front coral clumps in frontCoral hide mid-lane (and back-lane) fish; the sand lip, algae tufts and plant cluster in foreground sit in front of every lane. Flat sprite bottoms end at y 1060, inside the solid sand. Within a layer, decor draws in array order. Colors are hex strings because JSON integers cannot hold the 32-bit RGBA values.",
