  "seaweed": {
    "_notes": "P1.4 segmented seaweed (components/Seaweed): one Seaweed component per stalk, placed in its layer with its base at (x, y). segmentUris run base to tip (tools/art/seaweed.py); each Poster is segmentSize and the next segment starts segmentStep px higher, so joints overlap by segmentSize[1] - segmentStep px. Segment k swings amplitudeDeg * (0.5 + 0.5 * k / (n - 1)) degrees with a lag of k * phaseStepDeg, so the bend travels up the stalk over period seconds. The twelve segments make a 680 px blade at scale 1 (P1.4 made it 400 px); with phaseStepDeg 25 the stalk holds about three quarters of a wave and the tip swings about 8% of the blade height either side. The tallest tip (weedC) reaches about y 270, well clear of the y 0-120 surface band the drift spec compares. scale must stay positive (fidelity F4). tint is a 0xRRGGBBAA multiply.",
