  "population": {
    "_notes": "Tank fish (P2.7). ReefTank builds one FishBrain per lane that has fish, inside that lane's Group, and one School in school.lane. Each gets the lane rect from layers[].lane.rect and the world below as overrides on brainUri/behaviorUri/schoolUri, which keep the motion parameters and the species-to-kind map. Lane scale and tint are applied per fish (scale about the rig mirror_center, tint as Poster blendColor). Positions are design pixels of the fish anchor, re-measured (P1.8) on the composed day tank (backdrop plus the P1.7 decor at camera offset 0). ellipses keep anchors off the backdrop rock and coral still visible above the decor strips: e0 arch top, e1 arch left pillar and left brain coral, e2 arch right pillar, e3 lettuce coral, e4 right brain coral, e5 far-right sea whip. Below them the strips hide fish instead: back-lane fish pass behind the mid coral and front clumps, mid-lane fish behind the front clumps. caves (royal gramma, back lane): each mouth is in water the back lane can see and each den is behind coral (the arch pillar hole, behind the front clump b1, behind b1_2), so the fish backs out of sight. rocks are graze points on visible rock or coral tops. band is the sand line in front of the reef for the mandarin, above the solid sand lip. occluders (P1.8) map a decor layer to rects where its art is at least 97% opaque (alpha >= 0.9), measured from the sprites; ?debug=1 in the preview draws them (red) with the ellipses (yellow). weave (P2.4, components/lib/weave.brs): listed species change between adjacent lanes only while their whole body is inside an occluder of a layer in front of both lanes, so back and mid swap behind the front clumps; mid and front only swap off screen. offscreenPx widens every lane rect by that many px on both sides (components/lib/scenecfg.brs sceneCfgLanes), so fish swim off the screen edges before lane-keeping turns them back, while spawns stay inside the rect; past either screen edge (plus the drift) every adjacent lane pair gets an off-screen weave gap, so fish may change lanes, depth included, while out of view. densities: per lane [{species, count}] plus the chromis school {lane, count}; ReefTank.density picks one (default normal, unknown names fall back to normal). nightSchool (per density, optional, { lane, count }): the flashlight fish group, a second School built last in that lane from nightSchoolUri (config/night_school.json); its species is nightOnly, so the members are hidden by day and fade in with the night level, and being built after every day fish it leaves the day fish, their seeds and their creation serials unchanged.",
